From: mscharged-port contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Drain native DVD commands before original reset
Upstream-base: d664382f57002fbff143911c81b06b7e7a4b3ab4
Classification: native DVD worker lifecycle and mounted-media state.

Provide original OSReset's __DVDPrepareReset/__DVDGetCoverStatus requests
under the existing Nod DVD device. Waiting commands are silently unlinked,
retaining their source states and caller-owned handles. An active command's
callback is cleared unless cancellation already began. Enable interrupts
before waiting for actual read/callback retirement, as the original SDK does.
Reject retained native guard/IRQ context before any reset mutation.

Serialize complete open/close/reset lifecycles through actual mounted-state
retirement; reject overlapping and callback-reentrant lifecycle requests.
Reject new read/seek admission throughout shutdown, including after the worker
join, until a successful remount explicitly starts the worker again. Normal
cancellation stays separate. Close joins the actual worker without detaching.

Native cover status observes an actually mounted Nod partition or unmounted
media, with BUSY during reset/close drain. It does not model optical timing.
No NL completion, owner free, ResetTask admission or terminal success is added.
The actual port CMake provider declares the shared native interrupt dependency.

